    "product_id": "03f14d5c-e65a-4c8d-91a6-ecedc61e89bd",
    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 131135\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n435 AM PDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Breezy south-southwesterly wind gusts will continue through the\n  week with dry conditions and near-normal temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...Through Friday\n\nA trough is deepening over the Pacific Northwest is pushing last \nweek's high pressure eastward.  The interaction between these two \nsystems resulted in an pressure gradient and offered strong winds \nfor much of Saturday. Winds ease into the late night but rebuild \nlate Sunday morning. Sunday afternoon will offer another batch of \nwidespread gusty winds peaking around 30 mph for most areas with some \nof the higher elevations and favored gaps and passes exceeding 35 \nmph. The pressure gradient reduces into the work week, but the \ninfluence of the trough will offer breezy afternoons through much of \nthe week. Temperatures will be moving closer to average due to this \npattern change, with a gradual cooling trend expected into the the \nmid-week. High temperatures will fall back to near average (90s to \nlow 100s). Low temperatures, however, will only see some slight \nreduction, staying around 5 degrees above average. Temperatures look \nto gradually increase again by the end of the work week as pressure \nbegins to increase.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast \nPackage...Southwesterly winds will strengthen by late morning, \nwith sustained wind speeds of around 15 knots with gusts up to 25 \nknots possible. Winds will weaken after sunset, but speeds remain \nover 10 knots with modest gusts between 15 and 20 knots through \nthe night. Speeds eventually fall to less than 10 knots early \ntomorrow morning. Skies are mostly clear aside from FEW high \nclouds. Temperatures exceed 100 degrees between 20Z and 00Z.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Gusty westerly to \nsouthwesterly winds will increase areawide by late morning, with \nsustained speeds generally 10 to 15 knots with gusts 20 to 25 \nknots. Winds should weaken but remain over 10 knots for most \nlocations after sunset. One exception is KDAG, where westerly \nwinds will gust to around 25 knots through the night. VFR skies \nwith no precipitation except for isolated showers and \nthunderstorms over northern Mohave County this afternoon.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Murdock\nAVIATION...Meltzer\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
